Subject: [PATCH v4 0/4] wifi: rtw89: monitor mode RX filter, injection, and restart fixes

This series fixes monitor mode reception, standalone raw frame
injection, and monitor interface restart on Realtek rtw89 devices.

Patch 1/4 retains FIF_CONTROL and FIF_PSPOLL in *new_flags and
clears the hardware multicast, address CAM match, beacon check, and
UID filter bits in the local rx_fltr value while
IEEE80211_CONF_MONITOR is active without mutating the baseline
rtwdev->hal.rx_fltr state.

Patch 2/4 converts rtwdev->pure_monitor_mode_vif to an __rcu pointer,
adds rtw89_recalc_pure_monitor_vif() across interface addition and
removal, and updates existing readers with RCU primitives in
preparation for lockless access from rtw89_ops_tx().

Patch 3/4 enables raw 802.11 frame injection on a standalone monitor
interface by resolving NULL or NL80211_IFTYPE_MONITOR vif pointers
via pure_monitor_mode_vif under rcu_read_lock(), validating frame
length against ieee80211_hdrlen(), mapping NL80211_IFTYPE_MONITOR to
RTW89_SELF_ROLE_AP so rtw89_mac_vif_init() initializes the firmware
MACID CCTL entry, handling short Control frames (< 24 bytes) and
injected Data headers safely, and fixing negative rate indices,
NO_ACK retry limits, and software sequence preservation in
rtw89_core_tx_update_injection().

Patch 4/4 restores hardware channel configuration and RF calibration
when monitor mode is restarted on an unchanged channel on non-chanctx
(Wi-Fi 6) chips.

Changes in v4:
- Use full legal name in From/Signed-off-by per DCO requirements.
- Retain FIF_CONTROL and FIF_PSPOLL in *new_flags and also clear
  B_AX_A_MC and B_AX_A_MC_LIST_CAM_MATCH in monitor mode so
  multicast frames are captured even without IFF_PROMISC.
- Split RCU conversion of pure_monitor_mode_vif into a dedicated
  preparatory patch (2/4), use RCU_INIT_POINTER(..., NULL) when
  clearing the pointer, and introduce rtw89_recalc_pure_monitor_vif()
  so pure_monitor_mode_vif is maintained across both interface
  addition and removal.
- Gate both !vif and vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_MONITOR through
  rcu_dereference(rtwdev->pure_monitor_mode_vif) in rtw89_ops_tx(),
  validate skb->len >= ieee80211_hdrlen(fc), and populate
  info->control.vif.
- Drop redundant rtw89_fw_h2c_join_info() calls from
  rtw89_ops_add_interface() and rtw89_ops_remove_interface();
  setting RTW89_SELF_ROLE_AP in rtw89_vif_type_mapping() is
  sufficient because rtw89_mac_vif_init() already issues join_info
  and rtw89_mac_vif_deinit() removes the firmware role.
- Handle injected 802.11 Control frames (< 24 bytes, e.g. ACK/RTS)
  and injected Data frames by routing non-Data frames via
  RTW89_CORE_TX_TYPE_MGMT, guarding hdr->seq_ctrl against Control
  and < 24-byte skbs, and skipping traffic_stats_accu,
  wow_parse_akm, btc_spec_pkt_notify, update_he_qos_htc, and
  update_ampdu_info on injected skbs.
- Preserve injected sequence numbers by clearing
  desc_info->upd_wlan_hdr, desc_info->hw_ssn_sel, and
  desc_info->hw_seq_mode when IEEE80211_TX_CTL_ASSIGN_SEQ is not
  set, and honor IEEE80211_TX_CTL_NO_ACK.
- Fix negative info->control.rates[0].idx handling in
  rtw89_core_tx_update_injection() when radiotap omits a rate field,
  using data_retry_lowest_rate and honoring
  IEEE80211_TX_CTL_NO_CCK_RATE.
- Move monitor restart channel restoration from
  rtw89_ops_add_interface() to rtw89_ops_config() under
  IEEE80211_CONF_CHANGE_MONITOR && !rtwdev->chip->support_chanctx_num
  && !rtw89_get_entity_state(), avoiding a redundant RFK on cold
  start and preventing -EOPNOTSUPP / WARN_ON(ret) in mac80211 when
  hw->conf.chandef is not yet initialized.
- Drop the inaccurate Fixes: tag from patch 4/4.

Changes in v3:
- Split into a patch series.
- Dropped direct register writes in favor of driver abstractions.
- Added RCU synchronization around pure_monitor_mode_vif.

Tested on RTL8852AE (PCIe 10ec:8852, fw 0.13.36.2) on Linux 7.1.5:
- Passive RX capture across 2.4 GHz and 5 GHz channels.
- Raw 802.11 Management, Control (10B ACK, 16B RTS), and Data frame
  injection with sequence number preservation and aireplay-ng -9.
- 25+ monitor interface stop/start and delete/recreate stress cycles
  with concurrent raw TX and zero kernel warnings.

Enver Ikromov (4):
  wifi: rtw89: fix RX filter configuration for monitor mode
  wifi: rtw89: protect pure_monitor_mode_vif with RCU
  wifi: rtw89: support raw frame injection on standalone monitor
    interface
  wifi: rtw89: restore channel after monitor restart on non-chanctx
    chips

